# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository, and checked out as LF.
#
# This is not tidiness. Without it, a clone on Windows with the default
# core.autocrlf=true rewrites every text file to CRLF on checkout — including
# docker/entrypoint.sh, whose shebang then reads `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r`. The Linux
# container looks for a program literally named "bash\r", the API exits 127 before
# printing anything useful, and `docker compose up` — the one documented command —
# fails on a fresh clone while working perfectly in the repository it was built in.
#
# Caught by cloning the repo and running it as a reviewer would, not by any test.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the files where CRLF is actively fatal rather than merely untidy.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
